######################################################################
### PARLEY: THE NEGOTIATING TABLE - MULTI-SELECT PANEL   (user item 2.2 + U1(a))
###
### A types-only file. NO registration in gui/scripted_widgets is needed
### (same reasoning as tnt_types.gui and tnt_panels.gui; proven by
###  MOD\3276373926\gui\00_jdb_bc_map_icon_layer.gui).
###
### WHAT IS IN HERE, AND WHO USES WHICH PART
###   1. two ROW types            - tnt_multi_row_title, tnt_multi_row_artifact
###   2. the COUNTER line         - tnt_multi_counter_line
###   3. the DOMAIN line          - tnt_multi_domain_line   (U1(a))
###   4. THE PANEL                - tnt_panel_multi, with the four block
###                                 names fixed by the GUI NAMING CONTRACT:
###                                 tnt_multi_title, tnt_multi_counter,
###                                 tnt_multi_available_list,
###                                 tnt_multi_chosen_list
###   5. SIX READY-MADE PANELS    - tnt_panel_multi_title_p / _title_r /
###                                 _claim_p / _claim_r / _artifact_p /
###                                 _artifact_r. Each fills all four blocks
###                                 and carries its own `visible`, so the
###                                 gui owner instantiates each with ONE
###                                 line inside blockoverride
###                                 "tnt_picker_panels".
###   6. SIX DEAL-SHEET GROUPS    - tnt_sheet_sel_title_p and friends, for
###                                 blockoverride "tnt_sheet_multi_p" /
###                                 "tnt_sheet_multi_r" in tnt_panels.gui's
###                                 tnt_deal_sheet (item 3.4).
### V13 USER ITEM 1 RETIRED THE CLAIM PAIR IN BOTH FAMILIES: four picker panels
### and four deal-sheet groups are live now (title x2, artifact x2). The claim
### types are commented out in place behind a tombstone, never deleted, and
### overlay index 7 is RETIRED, not free.
###
### The generic tnt_panel_multi is kept parameterised even though the six
### derived panels exist: the contract names its four blocks, a later item
### (prisoners, per defect D3's redesign, or spouses) will want the same
### shape, and the derived panels are nothing but six sets of
### blockoverrides on it.
###
### WHY THERE IS NO `down =` ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE
###   Because there is no membership datafunction in the engine - no
###   Scope.IsInList, no datamodel Filter / Where / Count
###   (00-ARCHITECTURE section 4.6). A row's COLUMN is its state: available
###   on the left, chosen on the right, and a click MOVES it. That is the
###   entire point of the two-list shape (30-V2-DESIGN section 1 row 2.2)
###   and it is why this panel needs no per-row test of any kind. The
###   shipped single-object picker rows DO carry
###   `down = "[ObjectsEqual( TntVar('tnt_title_p').Title, Title.Self )]"`
###   because with one slot the question "is this the chosen one" is
###   answerable; with a list it is not.
###
### R-LAYOUT, obeyed everywhere below (30-V2-DESIGN section 9 D2):
###   a direct child of hbox / vbox / flowcontainer carries NEITHER
###   `position` NOR `parentanchor`. Every icon, coat of arms, portrait and
###   glyph that needs centring sits inside a plain `widget` and is
###   anchored INSIDE that - vanilla's own stepper does exactly this
###   (GAME\gui\window_knights.gui:716-759: no anchors on the hbox
###   children, `parentanchor = center` only inside button_round at :731,
###   :755). The two panels' own `parentanchor = center` IS legal: their
###   parent is tnt_picker_overlay, a plain widget, which arranges nothing
###   (same as the shipped tnt_picker_panel, tnt_types.gui:1385-1389).
###
### R-SPILL, obeyed on every text widget that prints GAME text (item 3.2c):
###   `autoresize = no` + `layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding`, and the
###   inherited `elide = right` is never overridden. type text_single
###   inherits autoresize = yes (GAME\gui\preload\labels.gui:6-16) and a
###   self-resizing child of an hbox reports a minimum width equal to its
###   full text width, so one long duchy name would push the row's glyph
###   outside the column.
###
### R11: every row carries a FIXED size - PDX's own "This is required for
###   performance reasons", GAME\gui\window_epidemics.gui:449-450 - and no
###   GetScriptedGui appears in any visible or down. The only script values
###   read per frame are the panel's counter (1), its cap flag (1) and, in
###   the two title panels, the domain pair (4) - read once per PANEL, never
###   once per row.
###
### Every base type verified on disk while writing this file:
###   hbox / vbox / widget / icon               GAME\gui\preload\defaults.gui
###   text_single                               GAME\gui\preload\labels.gui:6
###   template tooltip_es                       GAME\gui\preload\defaults.gui:12
###   spacer / expand / divider_light           GAME\gui\shared\windows.gui:590 / :597 / :944
###   button_standard                           GAME\gui\shared\buttons.gui:153
###   button_standard_list                      GAME\gui\shared\buttons.gui:348
###   button_plus_small / button_minus_small    GAME\gui\shared\buttons_icons.gui:596 / :608
###   header_pattern                            GAME\gui\shared\windows.gui:683
###   scrollbox                                 GAME\gui\shared\lists.gui:3185
###     (its blocks: scrollbox_margins :3208, scrollbox_content :3213,
###      scrollbox_empty :3222 - which sits inside a text_single, which is
###      why the empty-state blockoverride sets `text` and `visible`)
###   coa_title_tiny                            GAME\gui\shared\coat_of_arms.gui:591
###   artifact_tooltip                          GAME\gui\cooltip.gui:5568
###   Window_Background / Window_Margins        GAME\gui\shared\windows.gui:144 / :122
###   Background_Area_Dark                      GAME\gui\shared\backgrounds.gui:51
######################################################################

types TwdMultiSelect
{

	####################################################################
	### 1. THE TWO ROW TYPES
	###
	### Both are twins of the shipped picker rows (tnt_types.gui:1487 and
	### :1526) so the two columns of this panel look exactly like every
	### other list in the mod, with three differences:
	###   * no `down` - see the header;
	###   * a GLYPH at the right end that says which way a click moves the
	###     object (+ in the available column, - in the chosen one);
	###   * the title row uses plain `coa_title_tiny`, not
	###     `coa_title_tiny_crown`, and wraps it - see the note below.
	####################################################################

	### TITLE / CLAIM ROW.
	###
	### THE COAT OF ARMS: plain coa_title_tiny inside an alwaystransparent
	### holder, with the position blockoverride.
	###
	### Three decisions in one widget, each with a reason:
	### (a) `coa_title_tiny` and not `coa_title_tiny_crown`. The crown
	###     variant re-shows the `crown` icon, a 22 px strip stacked above
	###     the 36 px CoA with spacing -4 (GAME\gui\shared\coat_of_arms.gui:591-655),
	###     i.e. 54 px of content in a 45 px row. Plain coa_title_tiny
	###     leaves the crown hidden and, because its flowcontainer is
	###     `ignoreinvisible = yes`, the hidden crown costs no height at
	###     all: the control is 36 px. The tier is not lost - it is what
	###     the coat of arms frame itself shows, and the CoA keeps its own
	###     LandedTitleTooltip.
	### (b) `blockoverride "position" { position = { 0 0 } }` is REQUIRED
	###     with the crown hidden: coa_title_tiny shifts its flowcontainer
	###     up by 10 px to make room for that crown (block "position" at
	###     :601-603), and with no crown the shift only pushes the CoA out
	###     of the row. That override is verbatim vanilla ON THIS VERY TYPE
	###     - GAME\gui\window_county_view.gui:3561-3565 and
	###     GAME\gui\window_travel_route_edit.gui:242-246.
	### (c) the `alwaystransparent = yes` holder. coa_title_tiny is a
	###     `button_group`, so left to itself it would swallow the click
	###     that is supposed to reach the row. alwaystransparent on the
	###     holder makes the whole subtree click-through, which is exactly
	###     what vanilla's own artifact row does with button_artifact
	###     (GAME\gui\interaction_templates.gui:517-533) and what this mod
	###     already does in tnt_chosen_button (tnt_panels.gui:118-124).
	type tnt_multi_row_title = button_standard_list
	{
		name = "tnt_multi_row_title"
		layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
		size = { 0 45 }
		using = tooltip_es

		block "tnt_multi_row_click" {}

		block "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" {}

		hbox = {
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			margin = { 10 0 }
			spacing = 10

			widget = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_coa_holder"
				size = { 36 100% }
				alwaystransparent = yes

				coa_title_tiny = {
					name = "tnt_multi_row_coa"
					parentanchor = center

					blockoverride "position"
					{
						position = { 0 0 }
					}
				}
			}

			text_single = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_text"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				autoresize = no
				text = "[Title.GetNameNoTooltip|U]"
				align = nobaseline|left
				default_format = "#high"
				alwaystransparent = yes
				fontsize_min = 12
				using = Font_Size_Medium
			}

			### The direction glyph. A plain widget holder again, both so it
			### may centre (R-LAYOUT) and so the glyph cannot eat the click.
			widget = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_holder"
				size = { 26 100% }
				alwaystransparent = yes

				block "tnt_multi_row_glyph"
				{
					button_plus_small = {
						name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_icon"
						parentanchor = center
						alwaystransparent = yes
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}


	### ARTIFACT ROW. Icon + name + rarity + glyph, i.e. the shipped
	### tnt_picker_row_artifact plus the glyph. The icon triple
	### (texture / frame / framesize 240) and `Artifact.GetRarityAndSlotType`
	### are copied verbatim from that row, which ships and runs.
	### artifact_tooltip on the row is what makes the real artifact tooltip
	### appear - the same tooltipwidget the shipped row carries.
	type tnt_multi_row_artifact = button_standard_list
	{
		name = "tnt_multi_row_artifact"
		layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
		size = { 0 45 }
		using = tooltip_es

		tooltipwidget = {
			artifact_tooltip = {}
		}

		block "tnt_multi_row_click" {}

		block "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" {}

		### USER ITEM 4, THE TRUNCATED ARTIFACT NAME. The fixed furniture in this
		### row is shrunk so the expanding name column gets the space: margin
		### 10 -> 6, spacing 10 -> 6, and the rarity column 120 -> 90 below.
		### With the panel at 900 the row is 369 px, so the name now gets
		### 369 - 12 (margin) - 32 (icon) - 90 (rarity) - 26 (glyph) - 18 (three
		### spacings) = 191 px, against 71 px before. Nothing is lost by trimming
		### rarity: the row already carries the full vanilla artifact_tooltip
		### above, and the icon draws its own rarity frame (Artifact.GetIconFrame).
		hbox = {
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			margin = { 6 0 }
			spacing = 6

			widget = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_artifact_icon_holder"
				size = { 32 100% }
				alwaystransparent = yes

				icon = {
					name = "tnt_multi_row_artifact_icon"
					size = { 32 32 }
					parentanchor = center
					texture = "[Artifact.GetIcon]"
					frame = "[Artifact.GetIconFrame]"
					framesize = { 240 240 }
					alwaystransparent = yes
				}
			}

			text_single = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_text"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				autoresize = no
				text = "[Artifact.GetNameNoTooltip]"
				align = nobaseline|left
				default_format = "#high"
				alwaystransparent = yes
				fontsize_min = 12
				using = Font_Size_Medium
			}

			text_single = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_rarity"
				### 120 -> 90, see the note on the hbox above. Stays autoresize = no
				### and stays FIXED-width: the name beside it is
				### layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding inside a list row, and a
				### variable-width sibling would make the row jump per artifact -
				### that is R-SPILL, the defect user item 3.2 was about.
				min_width = 90
				max_width = 90
				autoresize = no
				text = "[Artifact.GetRarityAndSlotType]"
				align = nobaseline|right
				default_format = "#weak"
				alwaystransparent = yes
				fontsize_min = 12
				using = Font_Size_Small
			}

			widget = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_holder"
				size = { 26 100% }
				alwaystransparent = yes

				block "tnt_multi_row_glyph"
				{
					button_plus_small = {
						name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_icon"
						parentanchor = center
						alwaystransparent = yes
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### 2. THE COUNTER LINE
	###
	### "Chosen: 2" on the left, and on the right a warning slot that is
	### PERMANENTLY HIDDEN as of the artifact-picker fix.
	###
	### THE CAP IS GONE. V4 removed the three-object cap from
	### tnt_multi_add_effect entirely (tnt_35_multiselect.txt: all four
	### terms behave alike), yet the stale tnt_cap_hit_claim/artifact_*
	### flags still fired at >= 3 selected and this line printed
	### tnt_err_too_many - domain-limit words - at a limit that no longer
	### exists (the user's "third artifact" bug). The window's instance-
	### level `visible = no` overrides could not silence it, because the
	### derived types' plain blockoverride CONSUMED the named block (a
	### block stays re-overridable only through the block-inside-a-
	### blockoverride form, see the header of type tnt_panel_multi below).
	### THE FIX: no derived type fills block "tnt_multi_cap_visible" any
	### more; the default below stays `visible = no`. The warning text and
	### the block are KEPT as the wiring point for any future, real cap -
	### wire it HERE in the derived types, never at the instantiation.
	### Rows are deliberately never greyed either way: that would need
	### `enabled = "[TntValid(...)]"` on every row of every list - a
	### scripted-gui evaluation per row per frame, which Law R11 forbids.
	###
	### The counter number cannot come from the GUI, because a loc key
	### cannot be handed a parameter from a `text =`. It therefore lives
	### INSIDE the loc string, exactly as this mod already does at
	### tnt_l_english.yml:247 -
	###   tnt_ctx_terms:0 "Terms on the table: [GetPlayer.MakeScope.ScriptValue('tnt_items_count_value')|0]"
	### which is why there are six tnt_sel_count_* keys, one per list.
	###
	### The 3 px vertical margin is what centres the text: R-LAYOUT forbids
	### `parentanchor = vcenter` on a child of this hbox, and an hbox lays
	### its children out at the cross-axis origin, so 26 - 2*3 = 20 px of
	### content for an 18 px line. Same trick as tnt_sheet_group
	### (tnt_panels.gui:226-256).
	####################################################################
	type tnt_multi_counter_line = hbox
	{
		name = "tnt_multi_counter_line"
		layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
		size = { 0 26 }
		maximumsize = { -1 26 }
		spacing = 8
		margin = { 4 3 }
		alwaystransparent = yes
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		text_single = {
			name = "tnt_multi_counter_text"
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			autoresize = no
			align = nobaseline|left
			default_format = "#medium"
			alwaystransparent = yes
			fontsize_min = 12
			using = Font_Size_Small

			### Forwarded to the panel as the contract block
			### "tnt_multi_counter" - see tnt_panel_multi. The inner and
			### outer names are DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT: the verified
			### block-inside-a-blockoverride form always renames
			### (GAME\gui\window_ledger.gui:3402-3407 declares
			### `block "scrollbox_empty_visibility"` inside
			### `blockoverride "scrollbox_empty"`), and a same-named nesting
			### is attested nowhere.
			block "tnt_multi_counter_inner"
			{
				text = "tnt_sel_count_title_p"
			}
		}

		### The cap warning SLOT - hidden by default and, since the cap's
		### removal, wired by nobody (see the section header above). Fixed
		### width; the expanding child above is the one that always stays
		### visible, so `ignoreinvisible = yes` on this hbox collapses this
		### widget cleanly instead of shifting anything (the failure mode
		### tnt_panels.gui:325-334 documents for the deal sheet).
		text_single = {
			name = "tnt_multi_cap_text"
			min_width = 300
			max_width = 300
			autoresize = no
			text = "tnt_err_too_many"
			align = nobaseline|right
			default_format = "#N"
			alwaystransparent = yes
			fontsize_min = 12
			using = Font_Size_Small

			block "tnt_multi_cap_inner"
			{
				visible = no
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### 3. THE DOMAIN LINE   (U1(a) - MANDATORY, see 30-V2-DESIGN row U1)
	###
	### One line per side: "Your domain after this deal: 5 / 4", turning
	### red when the side ends up over its limit.
	###
	### WHY IT IS HERE AT ALL. The vanilla grant-titles screen prints
	###   [GetResultingDomainSize] / [Actor.GetDomainLimit]
	### with a red warning above the limit (GAME\gui\interaction_grant_titles.gui:105,
	### :125). That window is 100% C++ and cannot be reused (30-V2-DESIGN
	### row U1 is RED), but the idea is free, and it stops being a nicety
	### the moment item 2.2 lets a player push three counties across the
	### table: every holding above the limit pays no tax and raises no
	### levies (GAME\localization\english\holdings_l_english.yml:20-31).
	###
	### The numbers come from tnt_54_multiselect_values.txt
	### (tnt_domain_after_p/_r_value, tnt_domain_limit_p/_r_value) and, like
	### the counter, they live inside the loc string because a `text =`
	### cannot pass a parameter to a loc key.
	###
	### The over-limit state is a SEPARATE widget rather than a
	### `default_format` swap, because a block can override properties but
	### the two states want different text as well as a different colour.
	####################################################################
	type tnt_multi_domain_line = hbox
	{
		name = "tnt_multi_domain_line"
		layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
		size = { 0 26 }
		maximumsize = { -1 26 }
		spacing = 8
		margin = { 4 3 }
		alwaystransparent = yes
		ignoreinvisible = yes

		widget = {
			name = "tnt_multi_domain_icon_holder"
			size = { 22 100% }
			alwaystransparent = yes

			icon = {
				name = "tnt_multi_domain_icon"
				size = { 20 20 }
				parentanchor = center
				alwaystransparent = yes
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/character_interactions/icon_transfer_county.dds"
			}
		}

		text_single = {
			name = "tnt_multi_domain_text"
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			autoresize = no
			align = nobaseline|left
			default_format = "#medium"
			alwaystransparent = yes
			fontsize_min = 12
			using = Font_Size_Small

			### Named _label, not _text: the widget above is already called
			### tnt_multi_domain_text and a block that shadows a sibling
			### widget's name is a reader trap even where the engine does
			### not care.
			block "tnt_multi_domain_label"
			{
				text = "tnt_domain_after_p"
			}
		}

		### The warning half. Shown only when that side is over its limit.
		text_single = {
			name = "tnt_multi_domain_warning"
			min_width = 260
			max_width = 260
			autoresize = no
			text = "tnt_domain_warning"
			align = nobaseline|right
			default_format = "#N"
			alwaystransparent = yes
			fontsize_min = 12
			using = Font_Size_Small

			block "tnt_multi_domain_over"
			{
				visible = no
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### 4. THE PANEL
	###
	### A vbox instantiated inside tnt_picker_overlay's block
	### "tnt_picker_panels", beside the shipped tnt_picker_panel instances.
	### The overlay itself is already gated on `TntOn('tnt_picker')`
	### (tnt_types.gui:1362) and swallows clicks, so a panel needs nothing
	### but its own two index tests.
	###
	### 900 x 700 (was 760 x 700), a shell of the same family as the
	### tnt_editor_panel that tnt_panels.gui reserves for the other compound
	### editors (tnt_panels.gui:949-953) - two side-by-side lists do not fit the
	### 540 px single-list panel.
	###
	### WIDTH WENT 760 -> 900 FOR USER ITEM 4. The artifact rows truncated
	### ("Znamya di ...bolshoi nastenn ..."): at 760 the name column was left
	### exactly 71 px once the 120 px rarity column, the 32 px icon, the 26 px
	### glyph, the row margin and three spacings had taken their share of 279.
	### Widening the panel is the half of the fix that helps BOTH columns and
	### BOTH row types; shrinking the artifact row's fixed furniture is the other
	### half, on the row itself. At 1920x1080 the panel is centred, so 900 px
	### still leaves ~500 px of map either side and nothing is clipped.
	### Width budget: 900 - 80 (Window_Margins) = 820; two columns at 405
	### with spacing 10; each scroll area 405 - 10 - 26 = 369 px of row.
	### Height budget: 700 - 38 (margins) - 50 (header) - 26 (counter)
	###   - 24 (spacing x4) - 52 (domain block, title panels only)
	###   - 42 (footer) = ~468 px of list, i.e. 10 rows of 45 visible.
	### That height is now a CEILING and not a demand - see the note on the
	### Window_Margins vbox inside the type.
	###
	### DELIBERATELY NOT Window_Decoration_Spike: that template injects
	### icon CHILDREN, which a vbox would lay out in its flow.
	### Window_Background contributes only a `background = { }` block, which
	### is not a flow child - proven at GAME\gui\activity_window_widgets\
	### funeral_deceased_selection_widget.gui:85-90 and already relied on by
	### tnt_picker_panel.
	###
	### THE `block` INSIDE A `blockoverride` FORM IS VERIFIED - do not
	### "simplify" the header. Declaring a block inside a blockoverride of a
	### reusable type, then overriding that inner block from another file,
	### is vanilla: `type vbox_ledger` declares
	###   blockoverride "scrollbox_empty" { block "scrollbox_empty_visibility" {} }
	### at GAME\gui\window_ledger.gui:3402-3407 and it is overridden from
	### GAME\gui\interaction_marriage.gui:474. Header-text case:
	### GAME\gui\cooltip.gui:6034 overridden at GAME\gui\window_court_positions.gui:621.
	### The shipped tnt_picker_panel uses the same two nestings.
	####################################################################
	type tnt_panel_multi = vbox
	{
		### V4 (user item 4): HEIGHT FOLLOWS THE CONTENT, WIDTH DOES NOT.
		### Same fix and same reasoning as tnt_picker_panel in gui\tnt_types.gui - a
		### fixed 700 px meant a list of two counties opened a near-full-screen panel.
		### The height leaves `size` and becomes a ceiling, so a vbox measures its
		### children; 700 stays as the maximum, so nothing that used to fit stops
		### fitting. The inner scrollboxes drop `layoutpolicy_vertical = expanding`
		### (an expanding child is what asked for the whole 700 in the first place)
		### and instead MEASURE THEIR ROWS under a cap - `autoresizescrollarea = yes`
		### + size { 0 0 } + min/max, the vanilla ledger pattern. A bare cap changes
		### nothing about the base scrollarea's fixed 100 px height (user item 17(a);
		### details on the boxes themselves).
		name = "tnt_panel_multi"
		parentanchor = center
		size = { 900 0 }
		maximumsize = { 900 700 }
		alwaystransparent = no

		using = Window_Background

		vbox = {
			using = Window_Margins
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			### NO layoutpolicy_vertical HERE - USER ITEM 4, and it is the one line
			### that defeated the V4 fix described immediately above. An expanding
			### child asks its parent for everything, so this vbox pinned the panel
			### at its 700 px maximum while the content needed about 463, and the
			### ~220 px of surplus was then divided between the two list columns'
			### head / divider / list slots. That is why "Dostupno" and "Vybrano"
			### rendered as tall empty boxes with the caption floating in the middle
			### of a ~99 px band and the list crammed at the bottom: the 26 px
			### caption was always 26 px, it was its SLOT that was wrong.
			### The scrollboxes below deliberately dropped this same policy for the
			### same reason; this line was the last thing overriding them.
			spacing = 6

			header_pattern = {
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding

				blockoverride "header_text"
				{
					### THE CONTRACT BLOCK.
					block "tnt_multi_title"
					{
						text = "tnt_picker_title_title"
					}
				}

				blockoverride "button_close_tooltip"
				{
					tooltip = "tnt_btn_close"
				}

				### The shipped closer, which clears tnt_picker and
				### tnt_picker_side (tnt_21_pickers.txt GROUP E). This file
				### adds no closer of its own.
				blockoverride "button_close"
				{
					onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_picker_close')]"
				}
			}

			### THE TWO CONTRACT BLOCKS "tnt_multi_counter" and
			### "tnt_multi_cap_visible" are declared HERE, inside the
			### counter line's own two blockoverrides, so a consumer of
			### tnt_panel_multi overrides them once at the panel level and
			### never has to know that a counter line exists.
			tnt_multi_counter_line = {
				name = "tnt_multi_counter_row"

				blockoverride "tnt_multi_counter_inner"
				{
					block "tnt_multi_counter"
					{
						text = "tnt_sel_count_title_p"
					}
				}

				blockoverride "tnt_multi_cap_inner"
				{
					block "tnt_multi_cap_visible"
					{
						visible = no
					}
				}
			}

			####################################################################
			### V4: THE POINTS LINE. What this selection is worth, and what the whole
			### treaty stands at, side by side above the two columns.
			###
			### THE REQUEST: "insert a points counter for the deal into the multi-picker".
			### Two numbers rather than one, because they answer different questions and a
			### player choosing counties needs both: THIS TERM's price, which changes with
			### every click, and the TREATY's headline, which tells him whether he has
			### already done enough.
			###
			### THE LEFT NUMBER IS A BLOCK, because it differs per panel - a titles panel
			### must quote the titles value and a captives panel the captives value. Each
			### of the seven consumers overrides tnt_multi_points_value with its own
			### figure, and the _p ones pass the SCALED wrapper so the number is in the
			### same currency as the scales (see tnt_54_multiselect_values.txt).
			###
			### THE RIGHT NUMBER NEEDS NO BLOCK: tnt_ai_accept_value is the deciding value
			### of the whole treaty, identical for every panel.
			###
			### `alwaystransparent = yes` on both texts and on the row: this line is a
			### read-out sitting above clickable lists, and a non-transparent caption over
			### a control is the defect that cost a day (_docs/README.md item 4).
			####################################################################
			hbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_points_row"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				size = { 0 24 }
				maximumsize = { -1 24 }
				margin = { 4 0 }
				spacing = 8
				alwaystransparent = yes

				text_single = {
					name = "tnt_multi_points_label"
					autoresize = yes
					text = "tnt_multi_points_label"
					align = nobaseline|left
					default_format = "#weak"
					alwaystransparent = yes
					fontsize_min = 12
					using = Font_Size_Small
				}

				text_single = {
					name = "tnt_multi_points_figure"
					autoresize = yes
					align = nobaseline|left
					default_format = "#high"
					alwaystransparent = yes
					fontsize_min = 12
					using = Font_Size_Small

					block "tnt_multi_points_value"
					{
						text = ""
					}
				}

				expand = {}

				text_single = {
					name = "tnt_multi_deal_total"
					autoresize = yes
					text = "tnt_multi_deal_total"
					align = nobaseline|right
					default_format = "#weak"
					alwaystransparent = yes
					fontsize_min = 12
					using = Font_Size_Small
				}
			}

			divider_light = {
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			}

			### The two columns. A vbox as a direct child of an hbox is
			### legal - only a (flow)container rejects hbox/vbox children,
			### which is defect D3 (30-V2-DESIGN section 9 D3).
			hbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_columns"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				layoutpolicy_vertical = expanding
				spacing = 10

				############################################################
				### AVAILABLE
				############################################################
				vbox = {
					name = "tnt_multi_available_col"
					layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					layoutpolicy_vertical = expanding
					spacing = 4

					background = {
						using = Background_Area_Dark
					}

					### User item 6 pinned this head to one 26 px line (with no
					### vertical bound it was the only slack-absorbing child of an
					### expanding column, so an EMPTY list fed it up to 195 px and
					### the plate ballooned inversely to list fill; residual slack
					### now sits at the column bottom inside the shared dark plate
					### and both plates stay level). USER ITEM 8 extracted the
					### pinned shape into the shared type tnt_col_plate_head
					### (gui\tnt_types.gui section 12d) - the single-pick panels
					### wear the same head now, and the vanilla citations for the
					### pin moved to the type. The widget keeps its name; only
					### where its geometry is written changed.
					tnt_col_plate_head = {
						name = "tnt_multi_available_head"

						blockoverride "tnt_col_plate_head_text"
						{
							text = "tnt_picker_available"
						}
					}

					divider_light = {
						layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					}

					scrollbox = {
						name = "tnt_multi_available_scroll"
						layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
						### V4 item 4, corrected by user item 17(a): the cap alone was
						### not the fix. The base type is a scrollarea with a FIXED
						### size = { 100 100 } (GAME\gui\shared\lists.gui:3186), and a
						### scrollarea only sizes to its content with
						### `autoresizescrollarea = yes` - a bare cap left this
						### viewport pinned at ~2 rows while the dark column plates
						### stretched. Full vanilla ledger pattern instead
						### (GAME\gui\window_ledger.gui:9405-9408): autoresize +
						### size = { 0 0 } to clear the inherited 100x100 + the 420
						### cap. The 225 floor is five 45 px rows, so a near-empty
						### list still reads as a list and the two columns' plates can
						### never differ by more than that band (minimumsize with -1:
						### GAME\gui\interaction_declare_war.gui:314).
						###
						### D3 BELT: the WIDTH half of the cap was -1, i.e. left to the
						### layout, and that is the axis that broke. 405 is this column's
						### own width straight out of the header budget (:513-514: 900 - 80
						### Window_Margins = 820, two columns of 405 with spacing 10), so it
						### never binds today - the bound on the empty label above is what
						### actually fixes D3. It is here so no future content can inflate
						### the panel sideways, exactly as 420 already forbids vertically:
						### the worst case becomes a clipped sentence instead of a header
						### that carries the close X off the screen.
						autoresizescrollarea = yes
						size = { 0 0 }
						minimumsize = { -1 225 }
						maximumsize = { 405 420 }

						### Item 3.2(b): explicit, never inherited. A row is
						### `layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding`, and the
						### inherited Scrollbox_Margins right margin of 20
						### (GAME\gui\shared\windows.gui:135-140) leaves the
						### row's right edge 8 px UNDER the 12 px scrollbar
						### (GAME\gui\shared\lists.gui:3253-3259). 26 clears
						### the bar with 14 px to spare; 10 on the left buys
						### width back. Same numbers as the shipped
						### tnt_picker_panel.
						blockoverride "scrollbox_margins"
						{
							margin_left = 10
							margin_right = 26
							margin_top = 8
							margin_bottom = 8
						}

						### D3: THE EMPTY LABEL IS BOUNDED HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE.
						### Vanilla's empty-state slot is a BARE text_single
						### (GAME\gui\shared\lists.gui:3218-3226 - block "scrollbox_empty"
						### lives INSIDE it), so it inherits autoresize = yes, elide = right,
						### alwaystransparent = no and Font_Size_Small (fontsize 15,
						### GAME\gui\preload\fonts.gui:16-20) from type text_single
						### (GAME\gui\preload\labels.gui:6-16). An autoresizing SINGLE-LINE
						### textbox demands its whole sentence on ONE line: a 155-character
						### string asks for ~1000 px in a column that has 369 (budget,
						### :513-514). Nothing upstream stops that demand - the box below is
						### size = { 0 0 } with -1 on the WIDTH axis of both bounds, and every
						### ancestor up to the panel is expanding with no maximum - so the
						### header grew with it and carried the close X off the panel
						### (buttons_window_control is parentanchor = top|right,
						### GAME\gui\shared\windows.gui:704-706). This is the file's own
						### R-SPILL rule (:63-68) applied to the one widget that escaped it.
						###
						### multiline + autoresize + max_width is vanilla's own shape for a
						### wrapping empty-state: GAME\gui\window_court.gui:300-306
						### (PRISON_EMPTY, max_width 400), GAME\gui\interaction_modify_vassal_window.gui:543-549,
						### GAME\gui\window_legends.gui:140-154. On a text_single specifically,
						### with this exact align: GAME\gui\window_artifact_details.gui:616-621
						### (align = nobaseline, multiline = yes, max_width = 240) and
						### GAME\gui\window_rally_points.gui:331-338 (the expanding twin);
						### all three on one textbox at GAME\gui\credits_window.gui:115-125.
						### The inherited elide = right is NOT a hazard - vanilla's own
						### type text_multi keeps elide = right beside multiline = yes
						### (GAME\gui\preload\labels.gui:19-31).
						###
						### THESE PROPERTIES SIT BESIDE THE NESTED BLOCK, NOT INSIDE IT, ON
						### PURPOSE: a derived panel's plain blockoverride CONSUMES the named
						### block (section 2 header, :313-318), so anything written inside
						### would be dropped by the four artifact/title panels below, which
						### set only text + visible. A plain property beside a nested block
						### inside THIS blockoverride is vanilla at
						### GAME\gui\window_ledger.gui:3402-3407.
						###
						### alwaystransparent = yes is the house rule, not decoration: the
						### inherited `no` made this ~1000 px caption mouse-opaque right
						### across the neighbouring column's rows (_docs/README.md item 4).
						### It also means this widget can never host a tooltip - do not hang
						### one here.
						###
						### 340 = the 369 px of row this column has, less slack.
						blockoverride "scrollbox_empty"
						{
							multiline = yes
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 340
							align = nobaseline|left
							alwaystransparent = yes
							fontsize_min = 12

							block "tnt_multi_available_empty"
							{
								text = "tnt_picker_empty"
								visible = no
							}
						}

						blockoverride "scrollbox_content"
						{
							### THE CONTRACT BLOCK. scrollbox_content takes
							### exactly ONE child (GAME\gui\shared\lists.gui:3182).
							block "tnt_multi_available_list"
							{
								spacer = {}
							}
						}
					}
				}

				############################################################
				### CHOSEN
				############################################################
				vbox = {
					name = "tnt_multi_chosen_col"
					layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					layoutpolicy_vertical = expanding
					spacing = 4

					background = {
						using = Background_Area_Dark
					}

					### User item 6 / user item 8: same shared 26 px head as
					### tnt_multi_available_head above (full rationale there and on
					### the type), so neither header can absorb column slack when
					### its list empties and the two columns cannot drift apart.
					tnt_col_plate_head = {
						name = "tnt_multi_chosen_head"

						blockoverride "tnt_col_plate_head_text"
						{
							text = "tnt_picker_chosen"
						}
					}

					divider_light = {
						layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
					}

					scrollbox = {
						name = "tnt_multi_chosen_scroll"
						layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
						### V4 item 4, corrected by user item 17(a): same autoresize +
						### floor + cap as the available list (rationale there), so
						### both boxes track their own rows inside the same 225..420
						### band and stay level. The 405 width cap is the D3 belt, argued
						### on the available box above; 405 is this column's own width.
						autoresizescrollarea = yes
						size = { 0 0 }
						minimumsize = { -1 225 }
						maximumsize = { 405 420 }

						blockoverride "scrollbox_margins"
						{
							margin_left = 10
							margin_right = 26
							margin_top = 8
							margin_bottom = 8
						}

						### D3: the empty label is bounded HERE and nowhere else - same
						### six properties, same reasons, same vanilla citations as the
						### available column above; read them there. They sit BESIDE the
						### nested block so the four derived panels, which override only
						### text + visible, can never drop them.
						blockoverride "scrollbox_empty"
						{
							multiline = yes
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 340
							align = nobaseline|left
							alwaystransparent = yes
							fontsize_min = 12

							block "tnt_multi_chosen_empty"
							{
								text = "tnt_picker_chosen_empty"
								visible = no
							}
						}

						blockoverride "scrollbox_content"
						{
							### THE CONTRACT BLOCK.
							block "tnt_multi_chosen_list"
							{
								spacer = {}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}

			### U1(a), AMENDED BY USER ITEM 17(b): THE DOMAIN COUNTER IS
			### TITLE-PICKER-ONLY.
			###
			### This block USED to ship the two counter lines as its default
			### content, gated on tnt_domain_shown_value - so every panel that
			### merely inherited the block (claim, artifact, prisoner) showed
			### the counter whenever a county- or barony-tier title was in the
			### deal. That was a design choice ("a claim panel is a fine place
			### to be reminded...") and the user has overruled it: the counter
			### appears ONLY where titles are picked. Hence an EMPTY default.
			### The two title panels below keep their explicit
			### blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain" pairs and show the readout
			### unconditionally while open; every other consumer inherits
			### nothing. The deal-reading counter in the CENTRE COLUMN
			### (tnt_panels.gui, gated on tnt_domain_shown_value) is a
			### separate, still-wanted feature and is not touched by this
			### ruling.
			block "tnt_multi_domain" {}

			### FOOTER. "Clear" empties this term; "Done" dismisses the
			### panel through the shipped closer. Both `expand` children
			### carry an explicit unique name: `type expand` hard-codes
			### `name = "expander"` (GAME\gui\shared\windows.gui:598) and two
			### same-named direct siblings make the engine log a
			### duplicate-child line naming this file, which the acceptance
			### bar forbids for tnt_ paths (same treatment as
			### tnt_prisoner_row in tnt_panels.gui - that type is RETIRED with the
			### prisoner terms, user item 7, but the rule it illustrates stands).
			hbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_footer"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				size = { 0 42 }
				maximumsize = { -1 42 }
				spacing = 10

				button_standard = {
					name = "tnt_multi_clear_button"
					size = { 200 34 }
					text = "tnt_btn_clear"
					using = tooltip_es

					block "tnt_multi_clear_click" {}
				}

				expand = {
					name = "tnt_multi_footer_pad"
				}

				button_standard = {
					name = "tnt_multi_done_button"
					size = { 200 34 }
					text = "tnt_picker_done"
					onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_picker_close')]"
				}
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### 5. THE SIX READY-MADE PANELS
	###
	### The gui owner adds SIX LINES inside blockoverride
	### "tnt_picker_panels" (gui\tnt_diplomacy_window.gui:1090) and deletes
	### the six shipped single-object tnt_picker_panel instances at the same
	### three indices:
	###     tnt_panel_multi_title_p = {}
	###     tnt_panel_multi_title_r = {}
	###     tnt_panel_multi_claim_p = {}      <- RETIRED, V13 user item 1
	###     tnt_panel_multi_claim_r = {}      <- RETIRED, V13 user item 1
	###     tnt_panel_multi_artifact_p = {}
	###     tnt_panel_multi_artifact_r = {}
	### FOUR PANELS, NOT SIX, SINCE V13 USER ITEM 1. The claim pair is commented
	### out below with its two instantiations in gui\tnt_diplomacy_window.gui - a
	### design refusal, not a bug fix: vanilla gates claim fabrication behind a
	### LEARNING investment (task_fabricate_claim,
	### GAME\common\council_tasks\00_court_chaplain_tasks.txt:1088). The two lines
	### are kept in this list rather than struck out so the allocation stays
	### legible; OVERLAY INDEX 7 IS RETIRED, not free, and is never reused.
	###
	### Panel visibility is a pure variable test - the frozen item index
	### (contract R0.8: 6 = title, 7 = claim RETIRED, 10 = artifact) plus the side.
	### No GetScriptedGui in any `visible`. EqualTo_CFixedPoint over a
	### MakeScope value is verbatim vanilla,
	### GAME\gui\activity_window_widgets\debate_success_chance.gui:137, and
	### is the form all ten shipped panels already use.
	###
	### EVERY instance overrides `name`: type tnt_panel_multi sets
	### name = "tnt_panel_multi" in its own body, and six same-named direct
	### siblings would make the engine log "Duplicate children with the same
	### name override previous widgets" six times - with tnt_ in the line.
	###
	### Each row's `datacontext = "[Scope.Title]"` / `"[Scope.Artifact]"`
	### unwraps the variable-list element; `size = { 0 45 }` is restated at
	### the item site because R11 wants it there too.
	####################################################################

	### 6 / side 0 - titles the PLAYER cedes.
	type tnt_panel_multi_title_p = tnt_panel_multi
	{
		name = "tnt_panel_multi_title_p"
		visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker'), '(CFixedPoint)6' ), EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker_side'), '(CFixedPoint)0' ) )]"

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_title" { text = "tnt_picker_title_title" }
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_counter" { text = "tnt_sel_count_title_p" }
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_points_value" { text = "[TntSV('tnt_shown_title_multi_p_value')|+=0]" }
		### No "tnt_multi_cap_visible" override: the cap is gone and the warning
		### slot must stay at its hidden type default (section 2 header).
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_clear_click" { onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_sel_title_p_clear')]"  tooltip = "tnt_btn_none" }

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_available_empty"
		{
			text = "tnt_picker_empty"
			visible = "[IsDataModelEmpty( TntList('tnt_list_title_p') )]"
		}
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_chosen_empty"
		{
			text = "tnt_picker_chosen_empty"
			visible = "[IsDataModelEmpty( TntList('tnt_sel_title_p') )]"
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_available_list"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_rows_avail_title_p"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 3
				datamodel = "[TntList('tnt_list_title_p')]"

				item = {
					tnt_multi_row_title = {
						name = "tnt_multi_avail_title_p_row"
						datacontext = "[Scope.Title]"
						size = { 0 45 }

						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_click" { onclick = "[TntPickTitle('tnt_sel_title_p_add')]" }
						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" { tooltip = "tnt_btn_add_term" }
					}
				}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_chosen_list"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_rows_chosen_title_p"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 3
				datamodel = "[TntList('tnt_sel_title_p')]"

				item = {
					tnt_multi_row_title = {
						name = "tnt_multi_chosen_title_p_row"
						datacontext = "[Scope.Title]"
						size = { 0 45 }

						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_click" { onclick = "[TntPickTitle('tnt_sel_title_p_remove')]" }
						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" { tooltip = "tnt_btn_remove_term" }
						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_glyph"
						{
							button_minus_small = {
								name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_icon"
								parentanchor = center
								alwaystransparent = yes
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}

		### U1(a): both sides' domains, because a title deal moves holdings
		### in both directions at once.
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_domain_block_title_p"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 2

				tnt_multi_domain_line = {
					name = "tnt_multi_domain_p"
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_label" { text = "tnt_domain_after_p" }
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_over" { visible = "[TntPos('tnt_domain_over_p_value')]" }
				}

				tnt_multi_domain_line = {
					name = "tnt_multi_domain_r"
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_label" { text = "tnt_domain_after_r" }
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_over" { visible = "[TntPos('tnt_domain_over_r_value')]" }
				}
			}
		}
	}


	### 6 / side 1 - titles the PARTNER cedes.
	type tnt_panel_multi_title_r = tnt_panel_multi
	{
		name = "tnt_panel_multi_title_r"
		visible = "[And( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker'), '(CFixedPoint)6' ), EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker_side'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ) )]"

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_title" { text = "tnt_picker_title_title" }
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_counter" { text = "tnt_sel_count_title_r" }
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_points_value" { text = "[TntSV('tnt_val_title_multi_r_value')|+=0]" }
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_clear_click" { onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_sel_title_r_clear')]"  tooltip = "tnt_btn_none" }

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_available_empty"
		{
			text = "tnt_picker_empty"
			visible = "[IsDataModelEmpty( TntList('tnt_list_title_r') )]"
		}
		blockoverride "tnt_multi_chosen_empty"
		{
			text = "tnt_picker_chosen_empty"
			visible = "[IsDataModelEmpty( TntList('tnt_sel_title_r') )]"
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_available_list"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_rows_avail_title_r"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 3
				datamodel = "[TntList('tnt_list_title_r')]"

				item = {
					tnt_multi_row_title = {
						name = "tnt_multi_avail_title_r_row"
						datacontext = "[Scope.Title]"
						size = { 0 45 }

						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_click" { onclick = "[TntPickTitle('tnt_sel_title_r_add')]" }
						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" { tooltip = "tnt_btn_add_term" }
					}
				}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_chosen_list"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_rows_chosen_title_r"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 3
				datamodel = "[TntList('tnt_sel_title_r')]"

				item = {
					tnt_multi_row_title = {
						name = "tnt_multi_chosen_title_r_row"
						datacontext = "[Scope.Title]"
						size = { 0 45 }

						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_click" { onclick = "[TntPickTitle('tnt_sel_title_r_remove')]" }
						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" { tooltip = "tnt_btn_remove_term" }
						blockoverride "tnt_multi_row_glyph"
						{
							button_minus_small = {
								name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_icon"
								parentanchor = center
								alwaystransparent = yes
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain"
		{
			vbox = {
				name = "tnt_multi_domain_block_title_r"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				spacing = 2

				tnt_multi_domain_line = {
					name = "tnt_multi_domain_p"
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_label" { text = "tnt_domain_after_p" }
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_over" { visible = "[TntPos('tnt_domain_over_p_value')]" }
				}

				tnt_multi_domain_line = {
					name = "tnt_multi_domain_r"
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_label" { text = "tnt_domain_after_r" }
					blockoverride "tnt_multi_domain_over" { visible = "[TntPos('tnt_domain_over_r_value')]" }
				}
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### RETIRED - THE GRANTED CLAIM ("Peredat pretenziyu"), BOTH OVERLAY PANELS.
	### V13 USER ITEM 1.
	###
	### The two types below are the term's picker panels at overlay index 7, sides
	### 0 and 1. They retire with the two rows that opened them
	### (gui\tnt_diplomacy_window.gui) and with the two instantiations in that same
	### file - a .gui type and its instantiation are a single atomic pair, in both
	### directions: an instantiation of an undefined type errors, and a type left
	### defined with no instantiation is dead weight that reads as an oversight.
	###
	### THIS IS A DESIGN REFUSAL, NOT A BUG FIX. Nothing here was broken. The
	### user's ruling: vanilla gates the MANUFACTURE of claims behind a LEARNING
	### investment - claims are fabricated by the Court Chaplain's council task
	### (task_fabricate_claim,
	### GAME\common\council_tasks\00_court_chaplain_tasks.txt:1088) and what comes
	### out of it is keyed to LEARNING (a duchy-tier claim only above
	### mediocre_skill_rating at :1120; vassal opinion and piety penalties below
	### high_skill_rating at :1126 and :1132). You invest in Learning, you staff a
	### chaplain, you wait years, and you accept the side effects. Buying a
	### finished claim at the negotiating table short-circuits all of it.
	###
	### NOTHING IS DELETED. DO NOT RE-ENABLE ONE HALF - every setter these panels
	### call (tnt_sel_claim_*_add / _remove / _clear) is retired with them, and the
	### two candidate lists tnt_list_claim_p/_r lose their filling effect.
	### OVERLAY INDEX 7 IS RETIRED, not free: never renumbered, never reused.
	### Full tombstone: TOMBSTONE C in gui\tnt_diplomacy_window.gui and
	### common\scripted_effects\tnt_32_apply.txt.
