				}
			}
		}
	}

	####################################################################
	### RETIRED - THE GRANTED CLAIM'S TWO DEAL-SHEET GROUPS.  V13 USER ITEM 1.
	###
	### Six groups became four. These two are commented out with their
	### instantiations in gui\tnt_panels.gui (tnt_sheet_group_claim_p / _r) - type
	### and instantiation are one atomic pair, and an instantiation of an
	### undefined type is an engine error.
	###
	### A DESIGN REFUSAL, NOT A BUG FIX. Vanilla gates the manufacture of claims
	### behind a LEARNING investment: they are fabricated by the Court Chaplain's
	### council task (task_fabricate_claim,
	### GAME\common\council_tasks\00_court_chaplain_tasks.txt:1088) and the outcome
	### is keyed to LEARNING (duchy tier only above mediocre_skill_rating at :1120;
	### vassal opinion and piety penalties below high_skill_rating at :1126, :1132).
	### Buying a finished claim across the table short-circuits that investment.
	###
	### THE TWO COUNT VALUES THE HEAD ROWS READ ARE THE ONE PART THAT SURVIVES, and
	### it is not an oversight: tnt_count_sel_claim_p_value / _r_value stay DEFINED
	### but gutted to a constant 0, because five localization keys resolve them by
	### name and the key set is pinned at 553 - a loc key whose ScriptValue target
	### does not exist prints raw. Nothing in this file reads them any more.
	###
	### NOTHING IS DELETED. DO NOT RE-ENABLE ONE HALF.
	### Full tombstone: TOMBSTONE C in gui\tnt_diplomacy_window.gui and
	### common\scripted_effects\tnt_32_apply.txt.
