	####################################################################
	### THE CHARACTER ROW (V4 item A1; the captive panel it was written for is
	### RETIRED - user item 7 - and commented out below).
	###
	### THIS TYPE IS SHARED AND STAYS LIVE. Its consumers today are the two courtier
	### panels, gui\tnt_panel_people.gui. It was introduced for the captive picker,
	### which is why the notes below still argue about captives; the argument holds
	### unchanged for any list of people.
	###
	### A third row type was needed because the two that exist unwrap the wrong thing -
	### tnt_multi_row_title reads Title, tnt_multi_row_artifact reads Artifact, and a
	### courtier (like a captive before it) is a Character. Everything else is copied
	### from the artifact row: same button_standard_list, same 45 px, same glyph block
	### so the chosen column can swap the plus for a minus.
	###
	### THE PORTRAIT IS A portrait_head_tiny AND NOT AN ICON. It is the one widget that
	### makes a list of people readable at a glance, and it is what vanilla's own
	### character lists use. It carries alwaystransparent = yes, like every decorative
	### widget in this mod - the mouse lesson of _docs/README.md item 4 cost a day and
	### applies to portraits as much as to text.
	###
	### THE RIGHT-HAND COLUMN SHOWS THE RANK, because rank is what the price of a
	### person is made of. The worked example was the captive ladder (10 base, +15 kin,
	### +10 titled, +15/+25/+40/+60 by tier), retired with that term; the courtier
	### panels keep the column for the same reason - a player choosing whom to hand
	### over should see why one person is worth several times another.
	####################################################################
	type tnt_multi_row_char = button_standard_list
	{
		name = "tnt_multi_row_char"
		layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
		size = { 0 45 }
		using = tooltip_es

		tooltipwidget = {
			# container_character_tooltip, NOT character_tooltip: the bare name has
			# zero definitions in this install (whole-tree search). The container
			# form is vanilla's real type (GAME\gui\cooltip.gui:1340), used exactly
			# this way at GAME\gui\window_army.gui:2038.
			container_character_tooltip = {}
		}

		block "tnt_multi_row_click" {}

		block "tnt_multi_row_tooltip" {}

		hbox = {
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
			margin = { 10 0 }
			spacing = 10

			widget = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_char_portrait_holder"
				size = { 32 100% }
				alwaystransparent = yes

				### USER ITEM 4 (icon overlap): the explicit size is the fix, not
				### decoration. type portrait_head_tiny ships size = { 64 64 }
				### (GAME\gui\window_ledger.gui:6867-6869), and this instance used to
				### carry no size of its own - so all 64 px rendered centred in this
				### 32 x 45 holder: 16 px into the row's left margin, 6 px under the
				### name text (spacing 10 minus the 16 px right overhang), and ~10 px
				### into the rows above and below. The type's own scissor = yes clips
				### ITS children to ITS frame, never the frame to the holder, so the
				### bleed was real. Every other head in this mod already carried an
				### explicit size (tnt_picker_row_char 38, tnt_prisoner_row 36 - that
				### type is now RETIRED, user item 7, but it was measured at 36 and
				### the survey stands, tnt_chosen_char 38); 32 matches this row
				### family's own icon column - the artifact twin's 32 px cell.
				portrait_head_tiny = {
					name = "tnt_multi_row_char_portrait"
					size = { 32 32 }
					parentanchor = center
					alwaystransparent = yes
				}
			}

			text_single = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_text"
				layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding
				autoresize = no
				text = "[Character.GetUINameNoTooltip]"
				align = nobaseline|left
				default_format = "#high"
				alwaystransparent = yes
				fontsize_min = 12
				using = Font_Size_Medium
			}

			text_single = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_rank"
				min_width = 120
				max_width = 120
				autoresize = no
				### GetPrimaryTitle.GetNameNoTooltip and NOT a tier name: there is no
				### GetHighestHeldTitleTierName, no GetTierName and no GetRankName in the
				### game at all - all three return zero matches across the shipped
				### interface. What vanilla actually prints for a character's standing is
				### the primary title's name (5 sites), and that reads better anyway:
				### "Duke of Bavaria" tells the player more than "Duke".
				### A landless captive simply prints nothing here.
				text = "[Character.GetPrimaryTitle.GetNameNoTooltip]"
				align = nobaseline|right
				default_format = "#weak"
				alwaystransparent = yes
				fontsize_min = 12
				using = Font_Size_Small
			}

			widget = {
				name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_holder"
				size = { 26 100% }
				alwaystransparent = yes

				block "tnt_multi_row_glyph"
				{
					button_plus_small = {
						name = "tnt_multi_row_glyph_icon"
						parentanchor = center
						alwaystransparent = yes
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}


	####################################################################
	### RETIRED - THE CAPTIVE SELECTION PANEL (overlay index 13, side 0).
	### USER ITEM 7.
	###
	### The mechanic was BUILT, SHIPPED AND PLAYED: a per-captive selection list
	### on the player's side with a rank ladder for a price (10 base, +15 kin,
	### +10 titled, +15/+25/+40/+60 by tier). It was CONSIDERED AND WITHDRAWN FOR
	### AN INDEFINITE PERIOD on the user's ruling.
	###
	### A REVIVAL MUST LEAN ON THE VANILLA PRISONER SYSTEM rather than on this
	### mod's own bookkeeping: vanilla owns ransom_cost_value, the ransom
	### interactions, the release on_actions and the opinion and hook consequences
	### each carries. The private rank ladder above is exactly the kind of parallel
	### pricing that made the term stop reading as diplomacy.
	###
	### THE ROW TYPE ABOVE (tnt_multi_row_char) IS DELIBERATELY NOT RETIRED - it is
	### SHARED with the two courtier panels in gui\tnt_panel_people.gui. Only this
	### panel is commented out. Overlay index 13 is RETIRED, not free, and side 1's
	### reservation for a partner-side twin is released with it.
	### Nothing is deleted; do not re-enable one half.
	### Full tombstone: common\scripted_effects\tnt_32_apply.txt.
	####################################################################
